<img width="350" height="490" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-350x490.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Grilled flank steak salad garnished with corn from the top view." style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-350x490.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-768x1075.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-1097x1536.jpg 1097w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-400x560.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-150x210.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad-735x1029.jpg 735w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-flank-steak-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" />
<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p>During the summer months, I try to avoid turning on the stove or oven. If I can make it on the grill, that is where you will find me, especially when peak summer produce is at its best. This marinated flank steak salad is the perfect way to celebrate the season in one big fresh bowl.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad-1200x800.jpg" alt="Grilled marinated flank steak salad from the top view." class="wp-image-82756" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-salad.jpg"></figure>



<p>For years, I grilled flank steak with just salt and pepper, but lately, I have been marinating it for a few hours, which really amps up the flavor. The rest is simple: toss in whatever summer produce you have on hand, such as tomatoes, corn, or radishes, and make it your own. But really, take my recipe as a place to start and make it your own.&nbsp;</p>



<p>It is a fantastic summer salad recipe you will want to make again and again.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-simple-ingredients-you-ll-need">Simple Ingredients You&rsquo;ll Need</h2>



<p>You&rsquo;ll find the full list of ingredients in the <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/grilled-flank-steak-salad/#wprm-recipe-container-82768">recipe card</a> below, but here are a few notes you need to bring this grilled steak salad to life:&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view." class="wp-image-82757" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-Ingredients.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Flank Steak:</strong>&nbsp;</p>



<p>I usually use about 1&frac12; pounds of flank steak. When buying flank steak to use in this salad, ask your butcher to give you a piece that is well marbled for the best flavor.&nbsp;</p>



<p>You can certainly keep it simple with a little salt, pepper, and olive oil, but I opted to use my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/flank-steak-marinade/">Flank Steak Marinade</a>, which only takes about an hour to work its magic.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Salad Dressing:</strong>&nbsp;</p>



<p>I&rsquo;m using my Lemon Balsamic Vinaigrette for this recipe because it pairs beautifully with the grilled steak and vegetables. If you&rsquo;re in the mood for something lighter, my Lemon Vinaigrette is a great option too. You can even make the dressing a day ahead and keep it in the fridge until you&rsquo;re ready to serve.</p>



<p><strong>For the Salad:</strong></p>



<p><strong>Lettuce:</strong> I like using romaine for the crunch, but any salad greens you have on hand will work. Arugula or a simple spring mix are great options, too. Just make sure they&rsquo;re thoroughly washed, dried, and chopped into bite-sized pieces.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Corn:</strong> I grill my corn on the cob right before grilling the flank steak, but any corn, whether it is thawed frozen corn or drained and rinsed canned corn, would work in this recipe.</p>



<p><strong>Tomatoes:</strong> I like using cherry tomatoes, but any tomato will work. Roma, heirloom, or any ripe summer tomato is a good option. If you&rsquo;re using cherry tomatoes, slice them in half or into quarters if they&rsquo;re too big. For other tomatoes, cut them into bite-sized pieces so they&rsquo;re easy to mix into the salad.</p>



<p><strong>Radishes:</strong>&nbsp; I use regular red radishes, but any variety works. Just slice them thinly so the acid in the dressing can cut through their bitterness and give them a lightly pickled taste.</p>



<p><strong>Scallions:</strong> I opted for thinly sliced green onions (including both the white and green parts) for their milder flavor. But if you&rsquo;re after something with more bite, thinly sliced red onions are a great option.</p>



<p><strong>Avocado:</strong> Choose a ripe avocado. I recommend adding it just before serving so it stays fresh and does not turn brown. You can slice or cube it depending on your preference.</p>



<p><strong>Cheese:</strong> I used fresh mozzarella for its mild flavors. If you can get your hands on them, fresh mozzarella pearls are ideal, but you can also buy a whole mozzarella and cut it into bite-sized cubes.&nbsp;</p>



<p>Alternatively, for a bolder cheese option, crumbled goat cheese or blue cheese can also be used.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad">How To Make Grilled Flank Steak Salad?</h2>



<p>This marinated flank steak salad recipe consists of two main parts: first, we marinate the flank steak, then we grill it and assemble the salad. I usually marinate the steak the night before so it&rsquo;s ready to go, making this a perfect weeknight summer dinner.&nbsp;</p>



<p>Below are the step-by-step instructions, along with helpful notes from my recipe testing:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad.jpg" alt="Person making a flank steak salad and adding it into a bowl with the steak." class="wp-image-82759" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-steak-with-salad.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Make the Marinade:</strong> In a mixing bowl, combine all the marinade ingredients and whisk until smooth. I like to start with the wet ingredients first, then add the seasonings so everything blends evenly. Place the flank steak in a shallow glass dish or a resealable plastic bag.&nbsp;</p>



<p>Pour the marinade over the surface, ensuring it&rsquo;s evenly coated, then gently press or massage it in to allow the marinade to soak in. Cover and let it rest for at least 1 hour, or refrigerate up to overnight. Avoid marinating for more than 24 hours, as the acidity can break the meat down quite a bit and affect the texture.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad.jpg" alt="Person making salad dressing and grilling the meat." class="wp-image-82760" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/How-to-make-grilled-flank-steak-salad.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Make the Salad Dressing:</strong> In a small bowl, combine the balsamic vinegar, lemon juice, minced garlic, kosher salt, and pepper. Whisk to combine. Then, while whisking, slowly drizzle in the extra virgin olive oil until the dressing looks smooth and emulsified. Doing so helps the oil and vinegar come together without separating too quickly.</p>



<p>During my recipe testing, I&rsquo;ve found that using a combination of balsamic vinegar and lemon juice gives the dressing a nice balance of depth and brightness, complementing the balsamic flavors in the steak marinade.</p>



<p><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Grill the Steak:</strong> Preheat your grill to 500&deg;F. High heat is key here because it sears the steak, creating those beautiful grill marks. Scrape the grates clean to remove any leftover bits so the meat can get even contact with the heat, then coat them generously with olive oil. Place the steak directly on the grill and cook for about 4 to 5 minutes per side for medium-rare. Use an instant-read thermometer (affiliate link) to check doneness and avoid overcooking, especially with lean cuts like flank steak.</p>



<p>If you&rsquo;re not sure what temperature to aim for, here&rsquo;s a quick guide to help you cook your steak just the way you like it:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Medium-rare: </strong>130 to 135&deg;F (3 to 4 minutes per side)</li>



<li><strong>Medium:</strong> 140 to 145&deg;F (4 to 5 minutes per side)</li>



<li><strong>Medium-well:</strong> 150 to 155&deg;F (5 to 6 minutes per side)</li>
</ul>



<p>I usually aim for medium-rare to keep the steak juicy and tender. Going much past medium can cause it to dry out.</p>



<p><strong>Step 4 &ndash; Rest the Steak</strong>: Transfer the steak to a platter and cover with foil. Let it rest for at least 10 minutes while you prepare the salad. This allows the juices to redistribute so they stay in the meat when sliced, keeping every bite juicy and tender.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad.jpg" alt="A collage of images showing the dressing of the salad and the slicing of the grilled steak." class="wp-image-82761" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Steak-marinade-for-salad.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 5 &ndash; Assemble the Salad:</strong> In a large salad bowl, combine the chopped romaine lettuce, grilled corn, cherry tomatoes, thinly sliced radishes, thinly sliced green onions, avocado (sliced or cubed), and cubed mozzarella.&nbsp;</p>



<p>That being said, if you are assembling this salad a few hours in advance, it is best to add the avocado at the last minute to prevent it from browning. The same goes for the dressing; it is best to drizzle it right before serving to keep the salad crispy and fresh.</p>



<p>Taste and adjust the seasoning as needed. Sometimes all it needs is a pinch of salt or a touch more acidity to bring everything together.</p>



<p><strong>Step 6 &ndash; Slice the Steak:</strong> Slice the steak thinly (about &frac12; inch thick) against the grain. This means cutting across the natural lines you see running through the meat. Those lines are muscle fibers, and cutting across them makes each bite softer and easier to chew.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak.jpg" alt="The steak salad on a large plate from the top view." class="wp-image-82764" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-Flank-Steak-Salad-with-marinated-steak.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 7 &ndash; Arrange and serve:</strong> Arrange the meat on top of the salad and serve while still warm.</p>
</div>


