 data-uid="13"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1 &frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">lbs</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">flank steak</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">For The Salad Dressing:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="15"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">balsamic vinegar</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="16"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">lemon juice</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">freshly squeezed </span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="17"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">garlic clove</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">peeled and minced</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="18"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="19"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1/2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="20"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1/4</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">extra virgin olive oil</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">For The Salad:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="22"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">heads</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">romaine lettuce</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">rinsed, dried, and roughly chopped (about 6 cups)</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="23"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cups</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">corn kernels</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">grilled, or frozen, and thawed or canned and rinsed</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="24"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">cherry tomatoes</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">cut in half</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="25"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">small radishes</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">sliced thinly</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="26"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">scallions</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">chopped (both white and green parts)</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="27"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">ripe avocado</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">sliced</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="28"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">fresh mozzarella cheese </span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">cubed or crumbled goat cheese or blue cheese</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-82768-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82768-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82768"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To make the marinade, grab a large enough container that can accommodate your flank steak and place &frac14; cup of olive oil, &#8531; cup of soy sauce, &frac14; cup of apple cider vinegar, 2 tablespoons of lemon juice, 2 tablespoons of Worcestershire sauce, 1 tablespoon of Dijon mustard, 1 tablespoon of honey, 3 cloves of minced garlic, 1 teaspoon of sweet paprika, &frac12; teaspoon of ground cumin, &frac12; teaspoon of kosher salt, &frac14; teaspoon black pepper in it. Whisk until smooth.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Flank steak marinade being poured into a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Cover and let it marinate in the fridge for at least an hour or overnight (no more than 24 hours.)</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">While the meat is marinating, make the salad dressing. In a small bowl, place 3 tablespoons of balsamic vinegar, 2 tablespoons of freshly squeezed lemon juice, 1 clove garlic, peeled and minced, 1 teaspoon kosher salt and 1/2 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper. Give it a whisk. While still whisking, slowly add the 1/4 cup of extra-virgin olive oil. Whisk until fully incorporated and smooth. Set it aside.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing the dressing being made and the meat grilled." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Flank-Steak-and-corn-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To grill the steak, preheat a gas grill to 500 degrees &deg;F. Scrape the grill grates and coat them generously with the oil.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the flank steak on the grill and cook for 3-4 minutes on each side for rare (internal temperature is 130 to 135 &deg;F), 4-5 minutes on each side for medium (internal temperature is 136 to 145 &deg;F), or 5-6 minutes on each side for medium-well (internal temperature is 146 to 155 &deg;F).</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When it reaches your desired doneness, transfer the grilled flank steak to a platter and cover it with foil. Let it rest while you prepare the salad.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">To make the salad, place 6 cups of roughly chopped romaine lettuce, 2 cups of corn, 1 cup of chopped cherry tomatoes, 3 small sliced radishes, 3 thinly sliced green onions, 1 sliced avocado, and a cup of mozzarella pearls in a large salad bowl.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Person adding the dressing over the salad and the steak is sliced." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Grilled-steak-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-7" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Drizzle the dressing over the salad and toss to ensure that all of the ingredients are evenly coated. Add more seasoning to taste and adjust as needed.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82768-step-0-8" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Slice the steak against the grain (1/2-inch thick slices) and layer it over the salad just before serving.</span></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Grilled marinated flank steak salad from the top view." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-grilled-flank-steak-salad.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-82768-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe makes about 10 cups of salad that is ideal for 6 servings. The nutritional values below are per serving.</li>
<li><strong>Storing leftovers:</strong> If you know you&rsquo;ll have leftovers, I recommend storing the salad and the meat separately. If not, place the leftovers in the fridge for up to 3 days.</li>
<li><strong>Corn:&nbsp;</strong>You can use any corn you have on hand. Frozen (and thawed), Canned (and drained) or grilled fresh corn would all work. If you are planning to grill your corn, I recommend setting aside a bit more time as it takes longer for corn to grill (compared to the flank steak).</li>
</ul></div></div>
